# Airline checked-bag policy

<!-- rtdf-document-id: airline/section1_non_textual -->

> Module Section1NonTextual

> Using Definitions as W

Port of `data/_raw/deonticbench/airline/statutes/section1_non_textual` --- the
published American Airlines bag-fee policy, which is DeonticBench's *airline*
statute. Written from the statute text; the Prolog is the differential oracle,
never the source.

Unlike SARA, DeonticBench ships **no shared formalization**: each of the 300
cases carries its own self-contained Prolog program, statute rules and case
facts together. So the port is validated in two steps rather than one --- a
single generic Prolog oracle is checked against all 300 per-case programs, and
this Catala is then checked against that oracle over the seed worlds and over
fuzzed ones. See `deontic_scripts/README.md`.

## Carry-on bags

  "You're allowed 1 carry-on bag and 1 personal item in all cabins." The
  carry-on "cannot exceed 22 x 14 x 9 inches"; the personal item's
  "dimensions should not exceed 18 x 14 x 8 inches".

The corpus's Prolog reads this as a *property of a bag*, not as an allowance of
one: every item within the carry-on box is left uncharged, and the personal
item is never modelled at all. Measured over all 300 cases, exactly **one**
item fits the box in each, so no case can tell the two readings apart, and the
45 items that also fit the personal-item box are that same item every time.
The port follows the Prolog, which is the bug-compatible choice; the statute's
contrary reading is recorded in `deontic_scripts/DEVIATIONS.md` A1.

<!-- rtdf-block-id: airline/section1_non_textual:b0008; role: provision; provision-id: airline/section1_non_textual:p0006; source-lines: 20-20; relation: formalizes-preceding -->
```catala-metadata
## An ordinary bag must fit the box --- "cannot exceed 22 x 14 x 9 inches".
declaration ordinary_carry_on_fits content boolean
  depends on it content W.Item
  equals it.length <= 22 and it.width <= 14 and it.height <= 9
```

<!-- rtdf-block-id: airline/section1_non_textual:b0009; role: provision; provision-id: airline/section1_non_textual:p0007; source-lines: 23-23; relation: formalizes-preceding -->
```catala-metadata
## A soft-sided garment bag has its own limit and it is a sum.
declaration garment_bag_fits content boolean
  depends on it content W.Item
  equals (W.size_sum of it) <= 51
```

<!-- rtdf-block-id: airline/section1_non_textual:b0007; role: provision; provision-id: airline/section1_non_textual:p0005; source-lines: 17-17; relation: formalizes-preceding -->
```catala-metadata
## Items satisfying their provision-specific carry-on limit do not need to be
## checked. Exempt item kinds are handled separately by `item_exempt`.
declaration carry_on_fits content boolean
  depends on it content W.Item
  equals
    match it.kind with pattern
    -- OrdinaryBag: ordinary_carry_on_fits of it
    -- SoftSidedGarmentBag: garment_bag_fits of it
    -- DiaperBag: false
    -- BreastPump: false
    -- BreastMilkCooler: false
    -- ChildSafetySeat: false
    -- Stroller: false
    -- MedicalOrMobilityDevice: false
```

  "These don't count as your personal item or carry-on: diaper bags (1 per
  child), breast pump, small soft-sided cooler of breast milk, child safety
  seats, strollers and medical or mobility devices."

Not counting as the carry-on is not the same as being free: the statute puts
these outside the carry-on allowance, and says nothing about charging for them,
so the port carries them at no fee and does not count them as checked bags
either. The diaper bag is the one with a number attached, and the number is per
child, so it is the only exempt kind whose *position* among the items matters.

<!-- rtdf-block-id: airline/section1_non_textual:b0006; role: provision; provision-id: airline/section1_non_textual:p0004; source-lines: 10-14; relation: formalizes-preceding -->
```catala-metadata
## The diaper bag is allowanced rather than exempt --- one per child --- so it
## is false here and handled by position in `Trip.checked`.
## Which diaper bag this is, counting from the first: 1 for the first, 2 for
## the second.  "Diaper bags (1 per child)" is the only allowance in the
## carry-on section with a number, and the number is not per bag.
declaration diaper_rank content integer
  depends on t content W.Itinerary, pos content integer
  equals
    number of
      (list of j among (List.sequence of 1, (pos + 1))
       such that
         (match (List.nth_element of t.items, j) with pattern
          -- Absent: false
          -- Present content it: it.kind = W.ItemKind.DiaperBag))

declaration item_exempt content boolean
  depends on it content W.Item
  equals
    match it.kind with pattern
    -- BreastPump: true
    -- BreastMilkCooler: true
    -- ChildSafetySeat: true
    -- Stroller: true
    -- MedicalOrMobilityDevice: true
    -- DiaperBag: false
    -- OrdinaryBag: false
    -- SoftSidedGarmentBag: false
```

## Checked bags

The four fee tables are keyed by a *position* --- first, second, third,
fourth-and-beyond --- and a cabin column. Main Plus is not a column: the
footnote makes it Main Cabin plus one extra free bag, so it reads the Main
Cabin column and takes its allowance separately, below.

<!-- rtdf-block-id: airline/section1_non_textual:b0001; role: preamble-metadata; provision-id: none; source-lines: none; relation: preamble -->
```catala-metadata
declaration fee_cabin content W.Cabin
  depends on t content W.Itinerary
  equals
    match t.cabin with pattern
    -- MainPlus: W.Cabin.MainCabin
    -- BasicEconomy: W.Cabin.BasicEconomy
    -- MainCabin: W.Cabin.MainCabin
    -- PremiumEconomy: W.Cabin.PremiumEconomy
    -- Business: W.Cabin.Business
    -- First: W.Cabin.First

## The cabins that pay a first- or second-bag fee at all. Premium Economy,
## Business and First are $0 in every row of both tables; the rows where
## Premium Economy is written "---" (not offered) are read as $0 too, which no
## case reaches --- see DEVIATIONS A2.
declaration pays_early_bag_fee content boolean
  depends on t content W.Itinerary
  equals
    match (fee_cabin of t) with pattern
    -- BasicEconomy: true
    -- MainCabin: true
    -- PremiumEconomy: false
    -- Business: false
    -- First: false
    -- MainPlus: false

declaration us_pr content list of W.Country
  equals [W.Country.UnitedStates; W.Country.PuertoRico; W.Country.USVirginIslands]

declaration us_pr_canada content list of W.Country
  equals [W.Country.UnitedStates; W.Country.PuertoRico;
          W.Country.USVirginIslands; W.Country.Canada]

## "Between Guyana, Suriname and U.S., Puerto Rico, U.S. Virgin Islands,
## Canada, Mexico, Caribbean ..., Central America ..." --- its own row in both
## the First and Second Bag tables.
declaration guyana_suriname content list of W.Country
  equals [W.Country.Guyana; W.Country.Suriname]

## The Caribbean countries the corpus reaches. Both are named as exceptions in
## nearly every row that mentions the Caribbean, so they are only ever used
## through the explicit Cuba and Haiti tests below.
declaration caribbean content list of W.Country
  equals [W.Country.Cuba; W.Country.Haiti]

declaration andean content list of W.Country
  equals [W.Country.Colombia; W.Country.Ecuador; W.Country.Peru]

declaration other_south_america content list of W.Country
  equals [W.Country.Argentina; W.Country.Brazil]

declaration south_america content list of W.Country
  equals [W.Country.Colombia; W.Country.Ecuador; W.Country.Peru;
          W.Country.Argentina; W.Country.Brazil]

declaration europe_israel_qatar content list of W.Country
  equals [W.Country.Europe; W.Country.Israel; W.Country.Qatar]

## "To or from India, China, Japan, South Korea, Hong Kong" --- the row that
## carries the $450 overweight cell, which Australia and New Zealand do not.
declaration asia content list of W.Country
  equals [W.Country.India; W.Country.China; W.Country.Japan;
          W.Country.SouthKorea; W.Country.HongKong]

declaration australasia content list of W.Country
  equals [W.Country.Australia; W.Country.NewZealand]

## "To or from India, China, Japan, South Korea, Hong Kong, Australia and New
## Zealand" --- the row of the First, Second, Third and Fourth Bag tables.
declaration long_haul_pacific content list of W.Country
  equals [W.Country.India; W.Country.China; W.Country.Japan;
          W.Country.SouthKorea; W.Country.HongKong;
          W.Country.Australia; W.Country.NewZealand]

declaration to_cuba content boolean
  depends on t content W.Itinerary
  equals (W.destination_country of t) = W.Country.Cuba

declaration from_cuba content boolean
  depends on t content W.Itinerary
  equals (W.origin_country of t) = W.Country.Cuba
```

### First Bag

The table's rows are tried in the order the statute prints them, so that a
route matching two rows takes the earlier one. Only the Basic Economy and Main
Cabin columns are ever non-zero.

<!-- rtdf-block-id: airline/section1_non_textual:b0014; role: provision; provision-id: airline/section1_non_textual:p0012; source-lines: 36-50; relation: formalizes-preceding -->
```catala-metadata
declaration first_bag_fee content money
  depends on t content W.Itinerary
  equals
    if not (pays_early_bag_fee of t) then $0
    else
    # Within and between U.S., Puerto Rico and U.S. Virgin Islands
    if W.within of t, us_pr then $40
    # Within and between Canada and U.S., Puerto Rico and U.S. Virgin Islands
    else if W.within of t, us_pr_canada then $35
    # From ... to Cuba / From Cuba to ...
    else if to_cuba of t then
      (match (fee_cabin of t) with pattern
       -- BasicEconomy: $35
       -- MainCabin: $0
       -- PremiumEconomy: $0 -- Business: $0 -- First: $0 -- MainPlus: $0)
    else if from_cuba of t then $0
    # To or from Haiti
    else if W.touches of t, [W.Country.Haiti] then
      (match (fee_cabin of t) with pattern
       -- BasicEconomy: $35
       -- MainCabin: $0
       -- PremiumEconomy: $0 -- Business: $0 -- First: $0 -- MainPlus: $0)
    # Between Mexico, Caribbean (excluding Cuba/Haiti), Central America
    # (excluding Panama) and U.S., Puerto Rico, U.S. Virgin Islands, Canada
    else if W.touches of t, [W.Country.Mexico] then $35
    # Between Guyana, Suriname and U.S., Puerto Rico, USVI, Canada, Mexico,
    # Caribbean, Central America
    else if W.touches of t, guyana_suriname then $35
    # Between Panama, Colombia, Ecuador, Peru and ...
    else if W.touches of t, ([W.Country.Panama] ++ andean) then
      (match (fee_cabin of t) with pattern
       -- BasicEconomy: $45
       -- MainCabin: $0
       -- PremiumEconomy: $0 -- Business: $0 -- First: $0 -- MainPlus: $0)
    # Between South America (excluding Colombia, Ecuador, Peru, Guyana,
    # Suriname) and ...
    else if W.touches of t, other_south_america then
      (match (fee_cabin of t) with pattern
       -- BasicEconomy: $60
       -- MainCabin: $0
       -- PremiumEconomy: $0 -- Business: $0 -- First: $0 -- MainPlus: $0)
    # Between Israel / Qatar / Europe and ...
    else if W.touches of t, europe_israel_qatar then
      (match (fee_cabin of t) with pattern
       -- BasicEconomy: $75
       -- MainCabin: $0
       -- PremiumEconomy: $0 -- Business: $0 -- First: $0 -- MainPlus: $0)
    # To or from India, China, Japan, South Korea, Hong Kong, Australia and
    # New Zealand
    else if W.touches of t, long_haul_pacific then
      (match (fee_cabin of t) with pattern
       -- BasicEconomy: $75
       -- MainCabin: $0
       -- PremiumEconomy: $0 -- Business: $0 -- First: $0 -- MainPlus: $0)
    else $0
```

### Second Bag

<!-- rtdf-block-id: airline/section1_non_textual:b0016; role: provision; provision-id: airline/section1_non_textual:p0014; source-lines: 56-68; relation: formalizes-preceding -->
```catala-metadata
declaration second_bag_fee content money
  depends on t content W.Itinerary
  equals
    if not (pays_early_bag_fee of t) then $0
    # Within and between U.S., Canada, Puerto Rico and U.S. Virgin Islands
    else if W.within of t, us_pr_canada then $45
    # Between Honduras and U.S., Puerto Rico, USVI, Canada, Mexico, Caribbean
    # (excluding Cuba/Haiti), Central America (excluding Panama)
    else if W.touches of t, [W.Country.Honduras] then $45
    # Between Haiti and ...
    else if W.touches of t, [W.Country.Haiti] then $65
    # From all regions to Cuba / From Cuba to all regions
    else if to_cuba of t then $150
    else if from_cuba of t then $0
    # Between Mexico, Caribbean (excluding Cuba/Haiti) or Central America
    # (excluding Panama and Honduras) and U.S., Puerto Rico, USVI, Canada
    else if W.touches of t, [W.Country.Mexico] then $45
    # Between Panama and ...
    else if W.touches of t, [W.Country.Panama] then $100
    # Between Guyana, Suriname and ...
    else if W.touches of t, guyana_suriname then $45
    # Between South America (excluding Guyana, Suriname) and ...
    else if W.touches of t, south_america then $100
    # Between Europe, Israel, Qatar and ...
    else if W.touches of t, europe_israel_qatar then $100
    # To or from India, China, Japan, South Korea, Hong Kong, Australia and
    # New Zealand
    else if W.touches of t, long_haul_pacific then $100
    else $0
```

### Third Bag

Unlike the first two tables, this one charges every cabin. First is $0
everywhere except the domestic row.

<!-- rtdf-block-id: airline/section1_non_textual:b0018; role: provision; provision-id: airline/section1_non_textual:p0016; source-lines: 74-79; relation: formalizes-preceding -->
```catala-metadata
declaration third_bag_fee content money
  depends on t content W.Itinerary
  equals
    if W.within of t, us_pr_canada then $150
    else if (fee_cabin of t) = W.Cabin.First then $0
    else $200
```

### Fourth Bag +

  "$200" in every cell of every row.

<!-- rtdf-block-id: airline/section1_non_textual:b0019; role: provision; provision-id: airline/section1_non_textual:p0017; source-lines: 83-88; relation: formalizes-preceding -->
```catala-metadata
declaration fourth_bag_fee content money
  depends on t content W.Itinerary
  equals $200
```

<!-- rtdf-block-id: airline/section1_non_textual:b0001; role: preamble-metadata; provision-id: none; source-lines: none; relation: preamble -->
```catala-metadata
## The published fee for the checked bag in position `pos`, before any
## complimentary allowance is applied. This dispatcher contains no fee rule
## of its own; each arm calls the declaration under the corresponding table.
declaration table_fee content money
  depends on t content W.Itinerary, pos content integer
  equals
    if pos = 1 then first_bag_fee of t
    else if pos = 2 then second_bag_fee of t
    else if pos = 3 then third_bag_fee of t
    else fourth_bag_fee of t
```

### Complimentary Bags

  "^Main Plus includes 1 extra free checked bag in addition to the Main Cabin
  allowance (max of 2)."

The Main Cabin allowance is not stated as a number anywhere; it is read off the
tables, as the number of leading positions the Main Cabin column already prices
at $0. Domestically that is none, so Main Plus gets one free bag; on every
route where the Main Cabin first bag is free it is one, so Main Plus gets two
--- which is exactly where the footnote's cap binds.

Only the *count* moves. A free bag does not renumber the ones behind it: in
`airline_cases_complexity_0_airline_cases_12` a Main Plus passenger with four
checked bags pays $0 + $45 + $150 + $200, not $0 + $40 + $45 + $150.

<!-- rtdf-block-id: airline/section1_non_textual:b0015; role: provision; provision-id: airline/section1_non_textual:p0013; source-lines: 52-52; relation: formalizes-preceding -->
```catala-metadata
## Whether the first-bag table already gives Main Cabin a free bag.
declaration first_table_main_cabin_free content boolean
  depends on t content W.Itinerary
  equals (first_bag_fee of t) = $0

```

<!-- rtdf-block-id: airline/section1_non_textual:b0017; role: provision; provision-id: airline/section1_non_textual:p0015; source-lines: 70-70; relation: formalizes-preceding -->
```catala-metadata
## The repeated footnote after the second-bag table supplies the second step
## of the Main Cabin allowance used by Main Plus.
declaration second_table_main_cabin_free content boolean
  depends on t content W.Itinerary
  equals (second_bag_fee of t) = $0

```

<!-- rtdf-block-id: airline/section1_non_textual:b0001; role: preamble-metadata; provision-id: none; source-lines: none; relation: preamble -->
```catala-metadata
## Convert the two provision-local table facts to the number of leading bags
## already free in Main Cabin. This is glue, not an additional policy rule.
declaration main_cabin_allowance content integer
  depends on t content W.Itinerary
  equals if not (first_table_main_cabin_free of t) then 0
         else if not (second_table_main_cabin_free of t) then 1
         else 2

```

<!-- rtdf-block-id: airline/section1_non_textual:b0015; role: provision; provision-id: airline/section1_non_textual:p0013; source-lines: 52-52; relation: formalizes-preceding -->
```catala-metadata
declaration main_plus_allowance content integer
  depends on t content W.Itinerary
  equals
    match t.cabin with pattern
    -- MainPlus:
        (if (main_cabin_allowance of t) + 1 > 2 then 2
         else (main_cabin_allowance of t) + 1)
    -- BasicEconomy: 0
    -- MainCabin: 0
    -- PremiumEconomy: 0
    -- Business: 0
    -- First: 0
```

### Complimentary Bags, the rest of it

  "In some cases, you won't have to pay the fees for up to 3 bags ... If you
  qualify for complimentary bags based on your AAdvantage or oneworld status,
  the benefits are based on your highest status level at time of ticketing or
  check-in."

This is the part of the statute **no case in the corpus can state and no
reference program formalizes** --- 0 of 300, measured by
`check_shipped_rules.py`, because a case says only a cabin, a route, some boxes
and a price. It is written here anyway, on the reading below, and it is the one
part of the port with no oracle behind it of any kind: see DEVIATIONS C1.
Everything else in this file answers to something --- the 300 reference
programs, the rules recovered from them, RuleArena. This section answers only
to the reading below, and the differential suite can check it for consistency
between the two systems and for nothing more.

Two readings had to be chosen, and the statute settles both:

- **The grounds do not stack.** "the benefits are based on your **highest**
  status level" --- a passenger who is Executive Platinum *and* on military
  orders gets the better of 3 and 5, not 8. So the allowance is a maximum.
- **Ticketing and check-in resolve to the higher.** The statute's two bullets
  say what to do when they differ, and both come to the same thing: higher at
  ticketing, show the receipt and get it; lower at ticketing, current benefits
  apply. Either way the better of the two is what the passenger receives.

<!-- rtdf-block-id: airline/section1_non_textual:b0020; role: provision; provision-id: airline/section1_non_textual:p0018; source-lines: 92-92; relation: formalizes-preceding -->
```catala-metadata
declaration status_rank content integer
  depends on s content W.EliteStatus
  equals
    match s with pattern
    -- NoStatus: 0
    -- Gold: 1
    -- Platinum: 2
    -- PlatinumPro: 3
    -- ExecutivePlatinum: 4

```

<!-- rtdf-block-id: airline/section1_non_textual:b0021; role: provision; provision-id: airline/section1_non_textual:p0019; source-lines: 94-96; relation: formalizes-preceding -->
```catala-metadata

declaration effective_status content W.EliteStatus
  depends on t content W.Itinerary
  equals
    if (status_rank of t.status_at_ticketing) >= (status_rank of t.status_at_checkin)
    then t.status_at_ticketing else t.status_at_checkin

```

<!-- rtdf-block-id: airline/section1_non_textual:b0023; role: provision; provision-id: airline/section1_non_textual:p0021; source-lines: 100-104; relation: formalizes-preceding -->
```catala-metadata
## Gold, Ruby, and every higher status receive the first bag.
declaration status_first_bag_free content boolean
  depends on s content W.EliteStatus
  equals (status_rank of s) >= 1

```

<!-- rtdf-block-id: airline/section1_non_textual:b0025; role: provision; provision-id: airline/section1_non_textual:p0023; source-lines: 130-135; relation: formalizes-preceding -->
```catala-metadata
## Platinum and higher status receive the second bag.
declaration status_second_bag_free content boolean
  depends on s content W.EliteStatus
  equals (status_rank of s) >= 2

```

<!-- rtdf-block-id: airline/section1_non_textual:b0026; role: provision; provision-id: airline/section1_non_textual:p0024; source-lines: 137-143; relation: formalizes-preceding -->
```catala-metadata
## Platinum Pro and Executive Platinum receive the third bag.
declaration status_third_bag_free content boolean
  depends on s content W.EliteStatus
  equals (status_rank of s) >= 3

```

<!-- rtdf-block-id: airline/section1_non_textual:b0020; role: provision; provision-id: airline/section1_non_textual:p0018; source-lines: 92-92; relation: formalizes-preceding -->
```catala-metadata
## Assemble the consecutive status allowance from the three separately stated
## entitlements above.
declaration status_free_bags content integer
  depends on s content W.EliteStatus
  equals if status_third_bag_free of s then 3
         else if status_second_bag_free of s then 2
         else if status_first_bag_free of s then 1
         else 0

```

<!-- rtdf-block-id: airline/section1_non_textual:b0026; role: provision; provision-id: airline/section1_non_textual:p0024; source-lines: 137-143; relation: formalizes-preceding -->
```catala-metadata

## "Active U.S. military and / or dependents with ID traveling on orders
## (1st - 5th bags free of charge)"; "Active U.S. military with ID on personal
## travel" sits in the 1st--3rd tier.
declaration military_free_bags content integer
  depends on m content W.MilitaryStatus
  equals
    match m with pattern
    -- NotMilitary: 0
    -- OnOrders: 5
    -- PersonalTravel: 3

```

<!-- rtdf-block-id: airline/section1_non_textual:b0025; role: provision; provision-id: airline/section1_non_textual:p0023; source-lines: 130-135; relation: formalizes-preceding -->
```catala-metadata

## "Confirmed Domestic First customers, Confirmed Business customers,
## Confirmed Premium Economy customers" get the 1st and 2nd.
declaration standard_cabin_free_bags content integer
  depends on t content W.Itinerary
  equals
    match t.cabin with pattern
    -- First: 2
    -- Business: 2
    -- PremiumEconomy: 2
    -- BasicEconomy: 0
    -- MainCabin: 0
    -- MainPlus: 0

```

<!-- rtdf-block-id: airline/section1_non_textual:b0026; role: provision; provision-id: airline/section1_non_textual:p0024; source-lines: 137-143; relation: formalizes-preceding -->
```catala-metadata
## Flagship First and Flagship Business Plus customers get three bags.
declaration flagship_cabin_free_bags content integer
  depends on t content W.Itinerary
  equals if t.flagship
            and (t.cabin = W.Cabin.First or t.cabin = W.Cabin.Business)
         then 3 else 0

```

<!-- rtdf-block-id: airline/section1_non_textual:b0020; role: provision; provision-id: airline/section1_non_textual:p0018; source-lines: 92-92; relation: formalizes-preceding -->
```catala-metadata
## Take the better cabin benefit; the grounds do not stack.
declaration cabin_free_bags content integer
  depends on t content W.Itinerary
  equals if (flagship_cabin_free_bags of t) > (standard_cabin_free_bags of t)
         then flagship_cabin_free_bags of t
         else standard_cabin_free_bags of t

```

<!-- rtdf-block-id: airline/section1_non_textual:b0024; role: provision; provision-id: airline/section1_non_textual:p0022; source-lines: 106-128; relation: formalizes-preceding -->
```catala-metadata

## "or when traveling to these destinations (excluding Basic Economy)".
## Chile, El Salvador, Paraguay and Uruguay are in the statute's list and in no
## case's vocabulary; "Transatlantic" is read as Europe.
declaration complimentary_first_destinations content list of W.Country
  equals [W.Country.Argentina; W.Country.Australia; W.Country.Brazil;
          W.Country.China; W.Country.Colombia; W.Country.Cuba;
          W.Country.Ecuador; W.Country.Haiti; W.Country.HongKong;
          W.Country.India; W.Country.Israel; W.Country.Japan;
          W.Country.NewZealand; W.Country.Panama; W.Country.Peru;
          W.Country.Qatar; W.Country.SouthKorea; W.Country.Europe]

declaration destination_free_bags content integer
  depends on t content W.Itinerary
  equals
    if (fee_cabin of t) = W.Cabin.BasicEconomy then 0
    else if complimentary_first_destinations contains
            (W.destination_country of t) then 1
    else 0

```

<!-- rtdf-block-id: airline/section1_non_textual:b0023; role: provision; provision-id: airline/section1_non_textual:p0021; source-lines: 100-104; relation: formalizes-preceding -->
```catala-metadata

## "Eligible AAdvantage Aviator and Citi / AAdvantage cardmembers (on domestic
## American Airlines operated itineraries)" --- the 1st bag, domestic only.
declaration cardmember_free_bags content integer
  depends on t content W.Itinerary
  equals if t.cardmember and (W.within of t, us_pr_canada) then 1 else 0

```

<!-- rtdf-block-id: airline/section1_non_textual:b0020; role: provision; provision-id: airline/section1_non_textual:p0018; source-lines: 92-92; relation: formalizes-preceding -->
```catala-metadata

## The allowance the passenger actually receives: the best of the grounds, not
## their sum.
declaration free_checked_bags content integer
  depends on t content W.Itinerary
  equals
    combine all g among
      [main_plus_allowance of t;
       status_free_bags of (effective_status of t);
       military_free_bags of t.military;
       cabin_free_bags of t;
       destination_free_bags of t;
       cardmember_free_bags of t]
      in best initially 0
      with (if g > best then g else best)

## The fee actually charged for position `pos`: what the table prices it at,
## waived when the position falls inside the allowance.
##
## Stated in that order deliberately. Written the other way round --- $0 when
## the position is inside the allowance, the table otherwise --- it computes
## the same thing, but the allowance *shadows* the table, because
## `cabin_free_bags` grants First, Business and Premium Economy two bags that
## the tables already price at $0. The oracle's branch coverage caught it:
## those tables' clauses stopped being executed for those cabins entirely.
declaration position_fee content money
  depends on t content W.Itinerary, pos content integer
  equals
    if pos <= (free_checked_bags of t) then $0 else table_fee of t, pos
```

## Weight and Size

  "For all regions, except to / from Australia or New Zealand ... Weight:
  50 lbs. For First / Business, weight is 70 lbs for complimentary bags and
  50 lbs for excess charged bags. For all confirmed customers on flights to /
  from Australia or New Zealand: 70 lbs for complimentary bags and 50 lbs for
  excess charged bags."

So the 70 lb allowance attaches to a bag that is *complimentary* --- one whose
position is priced at $0 --- and only in First, Business, or on an Australia /
New Zealand route. Everywhere else the allowance is 50 lbs for every bag.

<!-- rtdf-block-id: airline/section1_non_textual:b0028; role: provision; provision-id: airline/section1_non_textual:p0026; source-lines: 148-151; relation: formalizes-preceding -->
```catala-metadata
## Outside Australia and New Zealand, First and Business complimentary bags
## receive 70 lb; every other checked bag receives 50 lb.
declaration cabin_complimentary_weight_allowance content integer
  depends on t content W.Itinerary
  equals
    if (fee_cabin of t) = W.Cabin.First
       or (fee_cabin of t) = W.Cabin.Business
    then 70 else 50
```

<!-- rtdf-block-id: airline/section1_non_textual:b0029; role: provision; provision-id: airline/section1_non_textual:p0027; source-lines: 153-155; relation: formalizes-preceding -->
```catala-metadata
## Australia/New Zealand gives every complimentary bag the 70 lb allowance.
declaration australasia_complimentary_weight_allowance content integer
  depends on t content W.Itinerary
  equals 70
```

<!-- rtdf-block-id: airline/section1_non_textual:b0001; role: preamble-metadata; provision-id: none; source-lines: none; relation: preamble -->
```catala-metadata
## Select the applicable provision without attributing the dispatcher itself
## to either mutually exclusive route rule.
declaration complimentary_weight_allowance content integer
  depends on t content W.Itinerary
  equals if W.touches of t, australasia
         then australasia_complimentary_weight_allowance of t
         else cabin_complimentary_weight_allowance of t
```

### Oversize Bags

<!-- rtdf-block-id: airline/section1_non_textual:b0034; role: provision; provision-id: airline/section1_non_textual:p0032; source-lines: 190-196; relation: formalizes-preceding -->
```catala-metadata
declaration oversize_fee content money
  depends on t content W.Itinerary, dim content integer
  equals
    if dim <= 62 then $0
    else if dim <= 65 then $30
    # Panama / South America (except Guyana / Suriname), and Europe, Israel,
    # Qatar, are the two $150 rows; every other row is $200.
    else if W.touches of t, ([W.Country.Panama] ++ south_america ++ europe_israel_qatar)
    then $150
    else $200
```

### Overweight Bags

  "More than one fee may apply per bag that exceeds standard dimensions for
  both weight and size. The higher fee between oversize and overweight
  applies, in addition to the checked bag fee."

The three weight bands are $30 (to 53 lbs), $100 (to 70), and $200 (to 100),
with two rows departing from them: to / from Cuba is $200 in the middle band,
and India / China / Japan / South Korea / Hong Kong is $450 in the top one.

Europe / Israel / Qatar and Australia / New Zealand read "Not accepted" in the
top band, which is not a fee at all, and above 100 lbs the table simply stops.
This function answers anyway, because it has to answer *something*, and what
carries the statute's meaning is `bag_accepted` below, false in exactly those
cases.

What it answers there is not arbitrary. The top band is carried upward rather
than capped, which is what `compute_answer.py` does in RuleArena --- the
independently written reference this corpus descends from, and the only
implementation that speaks where the statute is silent. A cross-check over the
fuzzed suite found the two worlds that distinguish the two readings, both with
a 101 lb bag. See DEVIATIONS A3.

<!-- rtdf-block-id: airline/section1_non_textual:b0031; role: provision; provision-id: airline/section1_non_textual:p0029; source-lines: 163-165; relation: formalizes-preceding -->
```catala-metadata
declaration slightly_overweight_fee content money
  depends on t content W.Itinerary, weight content integer, allowance content integer
  equals if weight > allowance and weight <= 53 then $30 else $0

```

<!-- rtdf-block-id: airline/section1_non_textual:b0032; role: provision; provision-id: airline/section1_non_textual:p0030; source-lines: 169-176; relation: formalizes-preceding -->
```catala-metadata
declaration medium_overweight_fee content money
  depends on t content W.Itinerary, weight content integer, allowance content integer
  equals if weight > allowance and weight > 53 and weight <= 70
         then (if (to_cuba of t) or (from_cuba of t) then $200 else $100)
         else $0

```

<!-- rtdf-block-id: airline/section1_non_textual:b0033; role: provision; provision-id: airline/section1_non_textual:p0031; source-lines: 180-186; relation: formalizes-preceding -->
```catala-metadata
declaration heavy_overweight_fee content money
  depends on t content W.Itinerary, weight content integer, allowance content integer
  equals if weight > allowance and weight > 70
         then (if W.touches of t, asia then $450 else $200)
         else $0

```

<!-- rtdf-block-id: airline/section1_non_textual:b0001; role: preamble-metadata; provision-id: none; source-lines: none; relation: preamble -->
```catala-metadata
## The weight bands are mutually exclusive. This dispatcher contains no
## statutory amount; each amount remains under its own table provision.
declaration overweight_fee content money
  depends on t content W.Itinerary, weight content integer, allowance content integer
  equals if weight <= 53
         then slightly_overweight_fee of t, weight, allowance
         else if weight <= 70
         then medium_overweight_fee of t, weight, allowance
         else heavy_overweight_fee of t, weight, allowance

```

<!-- rtdf-block-id: airline/section1_non_textual:b0033; role: provision; provision-id: airline/section1_non_textual:p0031; source-lines: 180-186; relation: formalizes-preceding -->
```catala-metadata

## A bag the policy will not carry at all: over 115 in, over 100 lbs, or in the
## 70--100 lb band on a route whose cell reads "Not accepted". No case in the
## corpus reaches any of these --- weights run 5--100 lbs and sizes 35--115 in,
## and no Europe or Australasia case has a bag over 70 lbs --- so this is the
## port's own reading and the oracle is written to match it. DEVIATIONS A3.
declaration bag_accepted content boolean
  depends on t content W.Itinerary, it content W.Item
  equals
    (W.size_sum of it) <= 115
    and it.weight <= 100
    and not (it.weight > 70
             and ((W.touches of t, europe_israel_qatar)
                  or (W.touches of t, australasia)))
```

## The charge for one bag, and for the trip

A bag's excess charge is the higher of its oversize and overweight fees, and
the overweight fee depends on whether this bag is one of the complimentary
ones. Since the passenger may say which bags those are, and the statute gives
no rule for choosing, the policy is read the way the corpus's Prolog reads it:
**the allocation that costs the passenger least.**

That minimisation needs no search. The base fees do not depend on the
allocation --- a complimentary bag pays $0 wherever it sits --- so the only
thing to choose is which bags get the 70 lb allowance, and the saving each bag
would make is independent of the others. Taking the largest savings is
therefore optimal, and the port ranks the bags rather than enumerating the
allocations, which is what `airline_cases_complexity_0_airline_cases_14` does
with `choose_two/3` and `min_list/2` over all pairs.

<!-- rtdf-block-id: airline/section1_non_textual:b0030; role: provision; provision-id: airline/section1_non_textual:p0028; source-lines: 159-159; relation: formalizes-preceding -->
```catala-metadata
declaration structure Bag:
  data position content integer
  data item content W.Item
  ## the excess charge if this bag is charged (50 lb allowance)
  data charged content money
  ## the excess charge if this bag is complimentary
  data complimentary content money

declaration bag_saving content money
  depends on b content Bag
  equals b.charged - b.complimentary
```

<!-- rtdf-block-id: airline/section1_non_textual:b0002; role: preamble-definitions; provision-id: none; source-lines: none; relation: preamble -->
```catala-metadata
declaration scope Trip:
  input itinerary content W.Itinerary
  ## The items that are not carry-on, in the order the case lists them.
  internal checked content list of W.Item
  internal bags content list of Bag
  ## How many of the checked bags are priced at $0.
  internal complimentary_count content integer
  output base_fees content money
  output excess_fees content money
  ## False when some bag exceeds what the policy will carry.
  output accepted content boolean
  output total_cost content money
```

<!-- rtdf-block-id: airline/section1_non_textual:b0007; role: provision; provision-id: airline/section1_non_textual:p0005; source-lines: 17-17; relation: formalizes-preceding -->
```catala
scope Trip:
  ## Itinerary quantities are physical facts. Negative prices, child counts,
  ## dimensions, or weights are outside this model's input domain.
  assertion itinerary.ticket >= $0
  assertion itinerary.children >= 0
  assertion
    for all it among itinerary.items we have
      it.length >= 0
      and it.width >= 0
      and it.height >= 0
      and it.weight >= 0

  ## Everything that is neither exempt, nor a diaper bag inside the one-per-
  ## child allowance, nor within a carry-on limit.  The diaper-bag allowance is
  ## the only rule here that has to count, so it is done by position: the first
  ## `children` diaper bags are free and any beyond them are checked.
  definition checked equals
    map each i among
      (list of j among (List.sequence of 1, ((number of itinerary.items) + 1))
       such that
         (match (List.nth_element of itinerary.items, j) with pattern
          -- Absent: false
          -- Present content it:
              not (item_exempt of it)
              and not (carry_on_fits of it)
              and not (it.kind = W.ItemKind.DiaperBag
                       and (diaper_rank of itinerary, j) <= itinerary.children)))
    to (match (List.nth_element of itinerary.items, i) with pattern
        -- Absent: W.Item { -- kind: W.ItemKind.OrdinaryBag
                            -- length: 0 -- width: 0 -- height: 0 -- weight: 0 }
        -- Present content it: it)

```

<!-- rtdf-block-id: airline/section1_non_textual:b0020; role: provision; provision-id: airline/section1_non_textual:p0018; source-lines: 92-92; relation: formalizes-preceding -->
```catala
scope Trip:
  definition complimentary_count equals
    number of (list of pos among
                 (List.sequence of 1, ((number of checked) + 1))
               such that (position_fee of itinerary, pos) = $0)

```

<!-- rtdf-block-id: airline/section1_non_textual:b0003; role: provision; provision-id: airline/section1_non_textual:p0001; source-lines: 2-2; relation: formalizes-preceding -->
```catala
scope Trip:
  definition base_fees equals
    Money.sum of
      (map each pos among (List.sequence of 1, ((number of checked) + 1))
       to (position_fee of itinerary, pos))

```

<!-- rtdf-block-id: airline/section1_non_textual:b0030; role: provision; provision-id: airline/section1_non_textual:p0028; source-lines: 159-159; relation: formalizes-preceding -->
```catala
scope Trip:
  definition bags equals
    map each pos among (List.sequence of 1, ((number of checked) + 1))
    to (match (List.nth_element of checked, pos) with pattern
        -- Absent:
             Bag { -- position: pos
                   -- item: W.Item { -- kind: W.ItemKind.OrdinaryBag
                                     -- length: 0 -- width: 0
                                     -- height: 0 -- weight: 0 }
                   -- charged: $0 -- complimentary: $0 }
        -- Present content it:
             Bag { -- position: pos
                   -- item: it
                   -- charged:
                        (if (oversize_fee of itinerary, (W.size_sum of it))
                            > (overweight_fee of itinerary, it.weight, 50)
                         then oversize_fee of itinerary, (W.size_sum of it)
                         else overweight_fee of itinerary, it.weight, 50)
                   -- complimentary:
                        (if (oversize_fee of itinerary, (W.size_sum of it))
                            > (overweight_fee of itinerary, it.weight,
                               (complimentary_weight_allowance of itinerary))
                         then oversize_fee of itinerary, (W.size_sum of it)
                         else overweight_fee of itinerary, it.weight,
                              (complimentary_weight_allowance of itinerary))})

  ## A bag takes the complimentary allowance when fewer than
  ## `complimentary_count` bags save strictly more by taking it --- ties broken
  ## by position, which cannot change the total because only the multiset of
  ## savings is summed.
```

<!-- rtdf-block-id: airline/section1_non_textual:b0030; role: provision; provision-id: airline/section1_non_textual:p0028; source-lines: 159-159; relation: formalizes-preceding -->
```catala
scope Trip:
  definition excess_fees equals
    Money.sum of
      (map each b among bags
       to (if (number of (list of o among bags
                          such that (bag_saving of o) > (bag_saving of b)
                                    or ((bag_saving of o) = (bag_saving of b)
                                        and o.position < b.position)))
              < complimentary_count
           then b.complimentary else b.charged))

```

<!-- rtdf-block-id: airline/section1_non_textual:b0033; role: provision; provision-id: airline/section1_non_textual:p0031; source-lines: 180-186; relation: formalizes-preceding -->
```catala
scope Trip:
  definition accepted equals
    for all b among bags we have bag_accepted of itinerary, b.item

```

<!-- rtdf-block-id: airline/section1_non_textual:b0003; role: provision; provision-id: airline/section1_non_textual:p0001; source-lines: 2-2; relation: formalizes-preceding -->
```catala
scope Trip:
  definition total_cost equals itinerary.ticket + base_fees + excess_fees
```
